            {
                "entry_id": "c6679691-cd12-359e-b8a8-7cc2b3c5bbad",
                "word": "dandy",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "7c80ea89-48b9-4518-9d71-658dbf8d25bd",
                        "entry_id": "c6679691-cd12-359e-b8a8-7cc2b3c5bbad",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "dandys"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "330931b3-f2f7-4550-aee1-4b44ef893652",
                        "entry_id": "c6679691-cd12-359e-b8a8-7cc2b3c5bbad",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "dandies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c72994d1-8a1c-3f75-b3dd-9c95a6f78bfc",
                        "entry_id": "c6679691-cd12-359e-b8a8-7cc2b3c5bbad",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Élégant se réclamant du dandysme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "37518b5d-7aae-4e3b-a5e0-f011e2bedeeb",
                                "sense_id": "c72994d1-8a1c-3f75-b3dd-9c95a6f78bfc",
                                "text": "Dès 1818, le vélocipède du baron Karl Drais von Sauerbroom avait été le support d'une mode éphémère et extravagante parmi les dandys et les aristocrates de Paris et de Londres."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a2fba37-183b-4b4b-95a2-12d9866f8bea",
                                "sense_id": "c72994d1-8a1c-3f75-b3dd-9c95a6f78bfc",
                                "text": "Hector Merlin et sa madame du Val-Noble, chez qui vont quelques grands seigneurs, les jeunes dandies et les millionnaires, ne t’ont-ils pas prié, toi et Coralie, à dîner ?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ba9d258f-f2cb-3013-83f1-fb03126d604d",
                        "entry_id": "c6679691-cd12-359e-b8a8-7cc2b3c5bbad",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Homme qui se pique d’une suprême élégance dans sa toilette et dans ses manières."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "737fa3b4-3fae-4ca1-bad1-d535e415e00d",
                                "sense_id": "ba9d258f-f2cb-3013-83f1-fb03126d604d",
                                "text": "Il raillait le luxe puéril des jeunes dandys qu’il eût pu imiter et qui se privaient des satisfactions nécessaires pour s’en donner de factices."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac2cefba-cd64-41ce-b693-506c68c74179",
                                "sense_id": "ba9d258f-f2cb-3013-83f1-fb03126d604d",
                                "text": "Le calme était déjà revenu dans ce dandy, le plus carré et le plus majestueux des dandys, lesquels — vous le savez ! — méprisent toute émotion, comme inférieure, et ne croient pas, comme ce niais de Goethe, que l’étonnement puisse jamais être une position honorable pour l’esprit humain."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4ca0b9e4-11e3-4d76-8b69-101b269ea0fb",
                                "sense_id": "ba9d258f-f2cb-3013-83f1-fb03126d604d",
                                "text": "Je rencontrais de bons bourgeois exactement habillés comme tous les bourgeois, sauf que la coupe de leurs vêtements donnait une assez pauvre idée du savoir-faire du seul et unique tailleur de l'Islande; aussi les dandies de l'endroit se font-ils habiller par les tailleurs et coiffer par les chapeliers de Copenhague."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "92ea2817-a7eb-4a73-95a1-ee5fc12d7a13",
                                "sense_id": "ba9d258f-f2cb-3013-83f1-fb03126d604d",
                                "text": "Vous croyez peut-être, d’après les racontars des envieux et des désœuvrés, que Boni de Castellane est un homme frivole, un élégant mondain, uniquement occupé de ses chaussettes de soie, de ses cravates et de ses étincelants chapeaux. C’est un dandy, certes, dans la bonne et balzacienne acception du mot, et il attache de l’importance aux choses de la toilette, dont je me suis moqué, pour ma part, profondément."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "42999e08-8f61-4d55-8fc5-0896e4dda8bf",
                                "sense_id": "ba9d258f-f2cb-3013-83f1-fb03126d604d",
                                "text": "Vous vous sentirez des âmes de dandy en montant le superbe escalier Napoléon III qui mène vers le lounge proprement dit, appelé le Salon Rouge en référence à la couleur des banquettes aux formes origamiques."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "be3e7a04-8665-4e17-816e-37ab0f0cfe52",
                                "sense_id": "ba9d258f-f2cb-3013-83f1-fb03126d604d",
                                "text": "Quand je regardais des extraits d’entrevues, je voyais cet homme qui portait des boutons de manchette avec l’élégance d’un dandy, et il m’est venu une image : Michel Louvain est notre Yves Montand. Une voix suave, une prestance, une classe, une dignité et une grande beauté."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6b3d067d-6b0e-499d-a35a-b98ecba45914",
                        "source_entry_id": "c6679691-cd12-359e-b8a8-7cc2b3c5bbad",
                        "target_lang_word": "dandy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dandy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8baa48b1-87c9-30f2-b9e5-dbf3510fa3a5",
                                        "entry_id": "bffcaec3-bc87-3529-8e2f-6efad543eaed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A man very concerned about his physical appearance, refined language, and leisurely hobbies, pursued with the appearance of nonchalance in a cult of self."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "911348f7-0fb3-4538-ba5e-6549192dcce5",
                                                "sense_id": "8baa48b1-87c9-30f2-b9e5-dbf3510fa3a5",
                                                "text": "The gallant young Indian dandy at home on furlough — immense dandies these — chained and moustached — driving in tearing cabs, the pillars of the theatres, living at West End Hotels, — […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74e3a444-8b19-4fcc-addf-0e4d1a406587",
                                                "sense_id": "8baa48b1-87c9-30f2-b9e5-dbf3510fa3a5",
                                                "text": "No town-bred dandy will compare with a country-bred one—I mean a downright bumpkin dandy–a fellow that, in the dog-days, will mow his two acres in buckskin gloves for fear of tanning his hands."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f3f7c6c-ed03-48bd-b1f0-9f42dc59e2d0",
                                                "sense_id": "8baa48b1-87c9-30f2-b9e5-dbf3510fa3a5",
                                                "text": "“Gerald Croft is an attractive chap about thirty, rather too manly to be a dandy but very much the easy well-bred young man-about-town.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5d6baf0-9e8a-3251-845a-771396951a5a",
                                        "entry_id": "bffcaec3-bc87-3529-8e2f-6efad543eaed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something excellent in its class."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2e7dccde-0155-35c9-91eb-01b8c6423f79",
                                        "entry_id": "bffcaec3-bc87-3529-8e2f-6efad543eaed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A yawl, or a small after-sail on a yawl."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7112f8bc-9af9-3eab-899c-8a789271d5b7",
                                        "entry_id": "bffcaec3-bc87-3529-8e2f-6efad543eaed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dandy roller."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6d07f21d-6acf-3c22-9ecd-7ee06a1becaf",
                                        "entry_id": "bffcaec3-bc87-3529-8e2f-6efad543eaed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small glass of whisky."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "UK",
                                            "archaic",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "797f0847-49ba-450b-aece-e486696e668e",
                                                "sense_id": "6d07f21d-6acf-3c22-9ecd-7ee06a1becaf",
                                                "text": "Somebody quite as notorious as Brummell, but whose follies have been far more mischievous; whose eloquence is great, but certainly not always refined; and to whose health many a dandy of whisky has been tossed off."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac82f916-6c3e-31e8-a20e-f8c8369f57ed",
                                        "entry_id": "bffcaec3-bc87-3529-8e2f-6efad543eaed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A horse-drawn railway carriage used on some branch lines."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "105d7f96-0a52-47d6-9045-aa9cdce12af6",
                                                "sense_id": "ac82f916-6c3e-31e8-a20e-f8c8369f57ed",
                                                "text": "Other notable instances of horse-drawn vehicles for passenger services were the dandies used on the two-mile branch to Inchture of the Perth-Dundee line of the Caledonian Railway […], and the 2½-mile branch of the North British Railway from Drumburgh to Port Carlisle. […] One of the Port Carlisle dandies was preserved at Waverley Station, Edinburgh, for several years, but is now in the Railway Museum at York."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "dandy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0114f691-05b3-303d-86f7-10b89f81c8a3",
                                        "entry_id": "00b8bdf9-8aef-3331-acb8-6aaf8c35cbc3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Like a dandy, foppish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "48ef18a6-a1e1-3dfd-865a-ba0b44d54be9",
                                        "entry_id": "00b8bdf9-8aef-3331-acb8-6aaf8c35cbc3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Very good; better than expected but not as good as could be."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00724ac5-d07e-41db-8db6-bae66e759bf2",
                                                "sense_id": "48ef18a6-a1e1-3dfd-865a-ba0b44d54be9",
                                                "text": "That's all fine and dandy, but how much does it cost?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3cd4d49f-9930-3883-ab31-0ea3d9a21a30",
                                        "entry_id": "00b8bdf9-8aef-3331-acb8-6aaf8c35cbc3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Excellent; first-rate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51b5c402-42ac-4709-b4b9-af2d58199ce8",
                                                "sense_id": "3cd4d49f-9930-3883-ab31-0ea3d9a21a30",
                                                "text": "What a dandy little laptop you have."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0629c63f-012c-4cb1-882b-bb0d47dc97a9",
                                                "sense_id": "3cd4d49f-9930-3883-ab31-0ea3d9a21a30",
                                                "text": "Grip Sures are dandy shoes for anything that comes along. Hiking, climbing, canoeing, around camp or in the gym — you can't have anything better."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d20d8e03-29b7-451a-9533-5dc5dc39645e",
                                                "sense_id": "3cd4d49f-9930-3883-ab31-0ea3d9a21a30",
                                                "text": "Its gonna be just dandy / The day I take my Candy / And make him mine all mine"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e21e67c-3796-47cc-8069-41ee26060bf2",
                                                "sense_id": "3cd4d49f-9930-3883-ab31-0ea3d9a21a30",
                                                "text": "A perfectly dandy cartoon feature, “The Jungle Book,” scooted into local theaters yesterday just ahead of the big day, and it's ideal for the children."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "dandy",
